  "question": {
    "text": "Time period of a simple pendulum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> inside a lift when the lift is stationary. If the lift moves upwards with an acceleration <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, the time period of pendulum will be :",
    "image": null
